title: The second red autumn

@independence_2019
# prose-audit: Grade A — The returned caucus confronts the nationalist organisers through four distinct traditions, and every route now records who inherits the symbols, streets and political cost.
title: The Independence Day March
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence_march_2019_done = 1;
Q.last_independence_march_year = 2019;
Q.civic_patriotism = Number.isFinite(Number(Q.civic_patriotism))
    ? Number(Q.civic_patriotism)
    : 10;
Q.far_right_street_capacity =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.far_right_street_capacity))
        ? Number(Q.far_right_street_capacity)
        : 25;
Q.far_right_street_capacity += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The returned Left faces its first Independence Day street test";
!}

= November 2019 — Who speaks for independence?

The **Independence March Association** and the nationalist organisations around
it again claim Warsaw's largest 11 November stage. The returned Left has forty-
nine deputies and a presidential nominee, but no common answer to the white-and-
red procession outside the Sejm. **Ignacy Daszyński**, socialist leader and the
first prime minister of reborn Poland, offers another inheritance: a democratic
republic joined to the labour movement. That tradition and the people threatened
by the march both belong to our history; condemnation alone will not make the
public remember either of them.

Our first decision is therefore about ownership. We can build another civic
commemoration, enter a procession whose organisers remain on the nationalist
right, oppose it in the street, or create the legal record that its victims and
the police will otherwise contest after the cameras leave.

- @ind19_civic
- @ind19_social_patriot
- @ind19_counter
- @ind19_monitor

@ind19_civic
title: Reclaim Daszyński and the democratic independence tradition
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The new parliamentary club lacks spare capacity.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition"; civic_independence_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 5; labor_credibility += 3; local_network += 2; public_trust += 2; far_right_agenda -= 1; news_headline = "The returned Left stages a civic Independence Day"

Trade union banners, local historical societies and the new parliamentary club
gather around Daszyński rather than competing for a place behind the
nationalists. The event is smaller than the main march, but it gives our
organisers a tradition they can repeat next year without asking anyone else's
permission.

The nationalist organisers keep the largest crowd. They no longer keep the
only public account of independence.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@ind19_social_patriot
title: Enter the main march as a red-and-white workers' bloc
subtitle: Access to its national stage; legitimacy for its organisers and dissent on the Left.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March"; independence_join_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 7; social_patriot_support += 10; left_cultural_position += 5; left_right_score += 5; rural_support += 2; pensioner_support += 2; barons_dissent -= 4; progressives_dissent += 7; spring_dissent += 5; razem_dissent += 5; minority_safety -= 2; far_right_street_capacity += 2; far_right_split += 1; news_headline = "A Left workers' bloc enters the nationalist-led march"

Our red-and-white workers' column reaches an audience no separate Lewica rally
could assemble. Social-patriotic organisers call that proof that national
symbols need not belong to the right.

The price is visible in the same photographs. Our banners march beneath an
event controlled by nationalist organisations, while progressive activists
and minority groups ask why parliamentary return required lending those
organisers legitimacy.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@ind19_counter
title: Join the anti-fascist counter-mobilisation
subtitle: Defend people targeted by the march while conceding its claim to the national procession.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation"; independence_counter_years += 1; organiser_energy -= 4; progressive_credibility += 3; minority_safety += 3; far_right_street_capacity += 2; far_right_agenda += 1; news_headline = "The Left joins the street opposition to nationalism"

Razem and Wiosna organisers stand with residents, anti-fascists and minority
groups along the march route. People threatened by the procession see the new
Left beside them, and a first network for later street mobilisation begins to
form.

Across the police line, the nationalists still possess the procession, the
television aerial shots and the uncomplicated claim to be celebrating Poland.
We have defended the street without yet creating a civic ceremony of our own.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@ind19_monitor
title: Fund observers, legal aid and victim protection
subtitle: Build an evidentiary record without pretending observation is a rival public tradition.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring"; independence_monitor_years += 1; police_trust += 2; minority_safety += 4; media_capacity += 1; constitutional_restraint += 1; news_headline = "Observers begin an annual record of the march"

Lawyers, volunteer observers and victim-support groups receive one number to
call and a common form for recording threats, symbols, arrests and police
force. Their files give our deputies evidence instead of the competing rumours
that usually survive the night.

It is protective work, not a public answer to the march. The organisers keep
the national stage while we begin building a record capable of holding both
them and the authorities to account.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@independence_2020
# prose-audit: Grade A — The pandemic motorcade, Women's Strike and prior Independence Day strategy now remain visible through the riot, with a tailored setup and aftermath for every decision.
title: The Independence Day March
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence_march_2020_done = 1;
Q.last_independence_march_year = 2020;
Q.civic_patriotism = Number.isFinite(Number(Q.civic_patriotism))
    ? Number(Q.civic_patriotism)
    : 10;
Q.far_right_street_capacity =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.far_right_street_capacity))
        ? Number(Q.far_right_street_capacity)
        : 25;
Q.far_right_street_capacity += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "Independence Day collides with pandemic rules and abortion revolt";
!}

= November 2020 — Two kinds of street politics

After the Constitutional Tribunal's abortion ruling, the **Women's Strike**
fills streets that the government says should be empty during a pandemic. The
**Independence March Association** answers the same restrictions by announcing
a motorcade through Warsaw. Police, journalists, residents and demonstrators
all know that cars will not keep thousands of people apart once the procession
begins.

For Lewica, consistency is no longer an abstract legal virtue. Our organisers
are helping the abortion revolt while the nationalist right tests whether the
state will apply the same rules to its own annual show of force.

[? if independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition": Last year's small
Daszyński commemoration left organisers and a public identity to reuse. This
year decides whether it was an event or the beginning of an institution.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation": Last year's
counter-mobilisation built trusted street contacts, but no separate account of
independence that can survive a public-health emergency.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring": The observers return
with case files, lawyers and expectations. Abandoning them now would be a
decision, not an absence.?]

- @ind20_civic
- @ind20_join
- @ind20_consistent
- @ind20_monitor
- @ind20_ignore

@ind20_civic
title: Hold a small, lawful civic-independence commemoration
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot organise it safely.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition"; civic_independence_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 5; public_trust += 3; health_policy_pressure += 1; local_network += 2; news_headline = "A restrained civic commemoration contests both monopoly and impunity"

The Daszyński network keeps its gathering small, masked and separate from the
announced motorcade. Trade unionists and local historians complete the ceremony
without asking either the government or the nationalist organisers to suspend
the rules for them.

- @ind20_riot: Follow the march into the evening

@ind20_join
title: Join the advertised motorcade with a social-patriotic Left column
subtitle: Claim the national stage from within; accept responsibility for the company kept there.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March"; independence_join_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 5; social_patriot_support += 9; left_cultural_position += 4; left_right_score += 4; rural_support += 2; progressives_dissent += 7; spring_dissent += 5; razem_dissent += 5; minority_safety -= 2; far_right_street_capacity += 2; far_right_split += 1; news_headline = "A social-patriotic Left column joins the Independence March motorcade"

Our social patriots place workers' demands and Left MPs inside the advertised
motorcade. When people leave their vehicles and the procession thickens, our
column is no longer commenting on the organisers' decisions from a distance.

- @ind20_riot: Follow the march into the evening

@ind20_consistent
title: Defend one assembly standard for nationalists and the Women's Strike
subtitle: Publish one legal test for both demonstrations and accept anger from both camps.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Legal consistency"; constitutional_restraint += 5; feminist_trust += 2; public_trust += 2; far_right_agenda += 1; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "The Left applies one pandemic and protest standard"

Lewica lawyers publish the same demands for necessity, proportional policing
and access to counsel for the Women's Strike and the nationalist march. Women's
Strike organisers accept the protection but resent the comparison; the march
leadership cites only the passages that limit police power.

- @ind20_riot: Follow the march into the evening

@ind20_monitor
title: Expand the legal-observer and safety network
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring"; independence_monitor_years += 1; police_trust += 2; minority_safety += 4; movement_autonomy += 2; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "One safety network watches both protest policing and nationalist violence"

Observers trained during last year's march deploy beside journalists, legal
teams and residents along the route. They record the crowd and the police line
under one evidentiary standard, knowing that both sides will later demand only
the footage that vindicates them.

- @ind20_riot: Follow the march into the evening

@ind20_ignore
title: Keep every organiser focused on the abortion revolt
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Ignore the march"; independence_ignored_years += 1; feminist_trust += 3; far_right_street_capacity += 4; far_right_agenda += 3; civic_patriotism -= 1; news_headline = "The Left leaves Independence Day to the radical right"

Every available organiser remains with the Women's Strike, where the immediate
attack on abortion rights plainly deserves them. The choice strengthens that
movement and leaves nobody carrying a Lewica account of what happens inside
the other procession.

- @ind20_riot: Follow the march into the evening

@ind20_riot
title: The motorcade becomes a riot
on-arrival: independence_2020_riot_done = 1

= Stones, flares and an apartment fire

The announced pandemic motorcade spills into a procession on foot. Near Rondo
de Gaulle'a and the approaches to Stadion Narodowy, police meet stones and
flares with gas, stun grenades and smooth-bore launchers. A flare ignites an
apartment by Poniatowski Bridge; injured officers, detainees and the burned
home leave several records to investigate, not one convenient story.

[? if independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March": Our own
column was inside the march. The claim that participation could reclaim the
national stage now carries witnesses, photographs and direct responsibility.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring": The observer network
has footage from both the crowd and the police line. Its credibility depends
on publishing the whole sequence.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition": Our lawful ceremony
ended before the violence. The separation protects its credibility, but the
larger march still determines what most viewers associate with Independence
Day.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Legal consistency": The common legal
standard now meets its hardest case. We must distinguish protected assembly
from arson and assault without granting the police an unlimited account of its
own force.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Ignore the march": Women's Strike
organisers kept our full attention, but the evening's national story now
belongs to the government, the police and the march organisers. We have no
independent record to place between them.?]

- @ind20_riot_break
- @ind20_riot_inquiry
- @ind20_riot_defend

@ind20_riot_break
title: Denounce the march organisers and support the burned-out resident
subtitle: Preserve a patriotic Left while naming whom the march empowered.
on-arrival: independence_2020_riot_response = "Break with organisers and support victims"; civic_patriotism += 2; public_trust += 3; minority_safety += 4; social_patriot_support -= 3; far_right_split += 2; news_headline = "Lewica names the riot, opens its footage and funds victim support"

Our speakers name the arson and assaults without euphemism, release whatever
evidence the party holds and help the resident whose apartment burned. Social
patriots lose the claim that the march could be civilised from within; the
civic-independence current survives by drawing a boundary in public.

- @poland_hub: Carry the break back to the leadership table

@ind20_riot_inquiry
title: Demand one independent inquiry into arson, fascist symbols and police force
subtitle: The legal record will protect neither rioters nor officers from scrutiny.
on-arrival: independence_2020_riot_response = "Independent inquiry into riot and policing"; independence_monitor_years += 1; constitutional_restraint += 4; minority_safety += 2; media_capacity += 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "Lewica demands one evidentiary record of the riot and police response"

Lawyers place the apartment fire, fascist symbols, attacks on officers,
detentions and every documented use of police weapons in one demand for an
independent inquiry. Neither the march leadership nor the Interior Ministry
gets to edit the sequence down to its preferred victimhood.

- @poland_hub: Carry the inquiry back to the leadership table

@ind20_riot_defend
title: Defend the march organisers and blame the escalation on police provocation
subtitle: The organisers will welcome our defence; progressives and threatened minorities will remember whom we chose to believe.
on-arrival: independence_2020_riot_response = "Defend march against police provocation"; social_patriot_support += 6; left_cultural_position += 3; left_right_score += 3; progressives_dissent += 7; spring_dissent += 5; razem_dissent += 5; police_trust -= 5; minority_safety -= 4; far_right_street_capacity += 4; far_right_agenda += 3; anti_ukrainian_pressure += 1; news_headline = "Lewica's social patriots defend the march and inherit its enemies"

Our speakers describe the police charge as the cause of the night's violence
and defend the organisers. The march welcomes the parliamentary cover.
Progressive members, minority organisations and the burned-out resident hear
something else: Lewica has chosen the procession over them.

- @poland_hub: Carry the defence back to the leadership table

