= Constructive roll call

**[+ confidence_candidate +] receives [+ confidence_yes +] votes—short of the
231 required to replace a government.** [+ confidence_no +] deputies vote
against and [+ confidence_abstain +] abstain.

[? if aug21_vonc_strategy = "Immediate opposition count": Lewica puts its name
and [+ constructive_sponsors +] signatures on the challenge. The opposition
clubs stand together, but Gowin's six departures never become the cascade our
whips needed. PiS turns survival into a warning to every deputy still wavering
on its benches.?]
[? if aug21_vonc_strategy = "All-opposition technical compact": Our whips find
a few votes beyond the democratic clubs without pretending that Konfederacja
has joined a common government. The broader count still falls short. Lewica
has demonstrated the outer limit of the anti-PiS majority—and must now answer
for every hand it was willing to count.?]
[? if aug21_vonc_strategy = "Opposition count filed without Lewica": KO files
after we decline to sponsor. Its deputies choose the candidate, arrange the
photograph and inherit the defeat. Lewica avoids ownership of an unwinnable
motion, but also proves that caution can surrender the whole opposition stage.?]

Morawiecki remains prime minister; Kosiniak-Kamysz never reaches the Palace.
Article 158 has done exactly what it says: measured a replacement majority in
the Sejm, not invited the president to invent one. The governing camp is
smaller than it was yesterday and, for this vote at least, still large enough.

- @aug21_constructive_return: Record the vote

