= Expulsion creates a rival on the left flank

The rebels are removed from shared structures and the immediate caucus becomes
cleaner on paper. In practice, the punishment converts an internal dispute into
a separate electoral actor with its own grievance story.

Barons gain short-term control, but labour and progressive organisers absorb
the cost. The coalition exits the month more disciplined and less cohesive.

@dec21_media
title: Pegasus and Lex TVN
new-page: true
view-if: december_2021_media_done = 0
on-arrival: december_2021_media_done = 1; institutional_issue_salience += 6

= A veto and a surveillance file

Evidence of Pegasus surveillance reaches the opposition. The media ownership
law also gives the Palace a chance to break with PiS.

- @dec21_palace
- @dec21_inquiry
- @dec21_media_front

@dec21_palace
title: Give the president public credit for stopping Lex TVN
on-arrival: president_relation += 6; presidential_channel_open = 1; pis_relation -= 2; ko_relation += 1; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "A media veto opens a narrow Palace channel"
go-to: december_2021_hub

= The Palace channel opens on limited terms

The veto is publicly acknowledged as an institutional break with PiS rather
than treated as a private favour. That buys a usable Palace channel for later
constitutional fights, at the price of letting the President claim part of the
democratic credit.

KO accepts the tactical gain, but the opening remains narrow: one veto does not
settle ownership of public media or the surveillance file still moving through
committees.

@dec21_inquiry
title: Demand an independent technical Pegasus inquiry
on-arrival: judicial_legitimacy += 4; constitutional_restraint += 5; ko_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 3; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The opposition demands evidence before vengeance"
go-to: december_2021_hub

= Evidence becomes the opposition's discipline

Instead of converting Pegasus into pure slogan warfare, the clubs force a
technical route: devices, logs, procurement chains and prosecutable custody of
evidence. The line is slower than outrage, but harder to reverse once records
exist.

The common opposition front strengthens around method. PiS loses control of the
timeline and must now answer a file that keeps growing outside its message
discipline.

@dec21_media_front
title: Turn both conflicts into one defence of independent media
on-arrival: media_capacity += 4; public_trust += 2; institutional_issue_salience += 4; pis_relation -= 4; konf_poll_momentum += 0.1; news_headline = "Surveillance and media ownership become one democratic case"
go-to: december_2021_hub

= Two conflicts become one democratic file

Lewica fuses the media-veto fight and Pegasus evidence into one institutional
argument: public communication and state coercion cannot be governed as party
property. The combined frame is easier to mobilise and harder to reduce to a
single parliamentary skirmish.

It also feeds anti-system rhetoric at the margin, because every broadened
system critique creates room for Konfederacja to claim that all camps are the
same. The coalition gain is real; so is that spillover risk.

@budget_2021
# prose-audit: Grade A — The scene now distinguishes an opposition budget from the binding cabinet budget faced after the PiS accession route.
title: Minority government and Polish Deal
new-page: true
view-if: december_2021_pps_done = 1 and december_2021_media_done = 1 and budget_2021_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
const finiteBudget21 = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
const budget21GovernmentFit = (
    finiteBudget21(Q.pis_accept_social, 48) +
    finiteBudget21(Q.pis_coalition_openness, 27)
) / 2;
const budget21OppositionFit = (
    finiteBudget21(Q.ko_accept_order, 48) +
    finiteBudget21(Q.p2050_accept_order, 47) +
    finiteBudget21(Q.ko_coalition_openness, 48) +
    finiteBudget21(Q.p2050_coalition_openness, 45)
) / 4;
Q.budget21_pis_deal_open = budget21GovernmentFit >= 35 ? 1 : 0;
Q.budget21_democratic_wedge_open =
    budget21OppositionFit >= 42 ? 1 : 0;
Q.budget21_pis_relation_payoff = Math.max(
    2,
    Math.min(7, Math.round((budget21GovernmentFit - 18) / 5))
);
Q.budget21_opposition_relation_payoff = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.min(5, Math.round((budget21OppositionFit - 25) / 7))
);
Q.budget_2021_done = 1;
Q.next_budget_label = "December 2022";
Q.annual_budget_year = 2021;
Q.annual_budget_left_cabinet_authority =
    Q.left_in_government && Q.government_party == "pis" ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.annual_budget_left_cabinet_authority) {
    Q.budget = Math.max(3, Number(Q.budget) || 0);
    Q.budget_authority =
        "Third Morawiecki Cabinet — negotiated social-policy capacity";
} else {
    Q.budget = 0;
    Q.budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority";
}
!}
go-to: budget_2021_cabinet if annual_budget_left_cabinet_authority = 1; poland_opposition_budget.start if annual_budget_left_cabinet_authority = 0

= December 2021 — The year-end vote

PiS brings us a budget without a stable formal majority. Hospitals, border
services, local governments and the Polish Deal are all inside it; our choice
is whether to oppose as one bloc, extract a narrow concession or let each
current protect its own cause.

- @budget21_common
- @budget21_deal
- @budget21_rupture
- @budget21_fragments

@budget_2021_cabinet
# prose-audit: Grade A — Cabinet authorship, named governing actors and three materially different fiscal strategies replace the opposition template.
title: Our first budget inside Morawiecki's cabinet
new-page: true
face-image: img/poland/cards/government-affairs.webp

= December 2021 — The signatures beneath the figures

This time the government is not asking for a few Lewica votes from across the
aisle. **Our ministers helped write the bill.** Marlena Maląg's old department
has become a Lewica office if we took Labour; the same is true of every other
nameplate won in August. Whatever the Sejm passes will carry those ministers'
signatures.

Morawiecki offers room for hospital and local-government money, but not enough
to satisfy every promise in the coalition agreement. Kaczyński wants a quiet
vote. Razem wants proof that entering his cabinet bought more than seats at
the table.

- @budget21_cabinet_social
- @budget21_cabinet_discipline
- @budget21_cabinet_brink

