The proposal guarantees that wages, pensions and public-service salaries do
not fall during the correction, then pays for that floor with a clearer
progressive schedule. Union offices can explain it without defending the
government's software or KO's return to flatter taxation.

It is still an opposition bill and a new budget promise. The costing gives
Lewica an answer; only a parliamentary majority could make it appear on a
payslip.

