Local organisations begin recruiting candidates under Lewica's own name and
Razem welcomes a campaign that will have to state what makes the Left distinct.
Tusk answers that separate lists are a luxury the opposition may discover it
could not afford.

The refusal preserves a political identity, not an electoral guarantee. Every
later poll near the threshold will reopen the argument in more frightened
terms.

