@may_2023
# prose-audit: Grade A — the live President, Tusk and the PiS commission now confront Lewica as institutions and rivals, while every route authors who owns the resistance and what the party sacrifices.
title: A commission built for one man
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const finiteLex = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
const lexRightsFit = (
    finiteLex(Q.ko_accept_rights, 55) +
    finiteLex(Q.psl_accept_rights, 34) +
    finiteLex(Q.p2050_accept_rights, 49)
) / 3;
const lexOrderFit = (
    finiteLex(Q.ko_accept_order, 51) +
    finiteLex(Q.psl_accept_order, 57) +
    finiteLex(Q.p2050_accept_order, 49)
) / 3;
const lexOpenness = (
    finiteLex(Q.ko_coalition_openness, 52) +
    finiteLex(Q.psl_coalition_openness, 36) +
    finiteLex(Q.p2050_coalition_openness, 48)
) / 3;
Q.lex_tusk_common_front_open =
    lexRightsFit >= 38 &&
    lexOrderFit >= 42 &&
    lexOpenness >= 38 ? 1 : 0;
Q.lex_tusk_relation_payoff = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.min(
        6,
        Math.round((lexRightsFit + lexOrderFit + lexOpenness - 85) / 18)
    )
);
Q.lex_tusk_2023_done = 1;
Q.sovereign_rename_2023_done = 1;
Q.suwerenna_renamed = 1;
Q.sovereign_poland_status =
    "Independent United Right partner under the Suwerenna Polska name";
Q.political_bulletin_pending = 1;
Q.political_bulletin_year = 2023;
Q.political_bulletin_title =
    "Solidarna Polska becomes Suwerenna Polska";
Q.political_bulletin_summary =
    "Ziobro remains leader; the allied party changes its name and sovereignty emphasis.";
const renamedSolidarna = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "solidarna";
});
if (renamedSolidarna) {
    renamedSolidarna.name = "Suwerenna Polska";
    renamedSolidarna.legal_status = "renamed allied party";
}
Q.institutional_issue_salience += 9;
Q.lex_tusk_presidential_status =
    Q.president_name == "Andrzej Duda"
        ? "Presidential signature promised"
        : "Presidential veto promised";
if (Q.president_name != "Andrzej Duda") {
    Q.constitutional_restraint += 2;
    if (Q.president_name == "Rafał Trzaskowski") {
        Q.trz_vetoes = (Number(Q.trz_vetoes) || 0) + 1;
    }
}
Q.news_headline = "The Russian-influence commission unifies the opposition";
!}

= May 2023 — A verdict before the election

The PiS majority passes a law creating a state commission to investigate
Russian influence and gives it the power to condemn public figures without a
criminal trial.
Donald Tusk—the KO leader, former prime minister and obvious target—calls it a
court assembled for his removal. [? if president_name = "Andrzej Duda":
President Andrzej Duda says he will sign the law.?][? if president_name !=
"Andrzej Duda": President **[+ president_name +]** says the commission cannot
take effect in this form and promises a veto.?]

Tusk has already summoned the opposition to Warsaw on 4 June, the anniversary
of the 1989 election. What began as his demonstration can now become a defence
of the democratic field itself. Lewica must help fill the streets without
vanishing into the political biography of the man most likely to lead them.

- @may23_front
- @may23_legal
- @may23_contingent
- @may23_caution

@may23_front
title: Join one democratic front and mobilise for 4 June
choose-if: lex_tusk_common_front_open = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The opposition can share a protest, but not yet a binding response.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ko_relation += Q.lex_tusk_relation_payoff;
Q.p2050_relation += Math.max(1, Q.lex_tusk_relation_payoff - 1);
Q.psl_relation += Math.max(1, Q.lex_tusk_relation_payoff - 2);
Q.june_march_preparation = 3;
Q.organiser_energy -= 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.news_headline = "The Left joins the common march against Lex Tusk";
!}

Lewica joins KO, Polska 2050 and PSL before the commission can sort its enemies
into separate files. The common declaration makes the 4 June march harder for
PiS to dismiss as Tusk's private grievance. It also gives Tusk the central
microphone; our reward is influence over the cause, not ownership of the day.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may23_legal
title: Lead a separate constitutional challenge
on-arrival: judicial_legitimacy += 5; constitutional_restraint += 5; ko_relation += 1; june_march_preparation = 1; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Left builds the legal case before the march"

Constitutional lawyers, former judges and our MPs turn the commission's powers
into a case the public can follow. The challenge denies PiS the language of a
mere party feud and gives Lewica an institutional role distinct from Tusk's.
It cannot, by itself, put a crowd on the streets before the law takes effect.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may23_contingent
title: Build a visible Left contingent inside the common march
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No capacity for a distinct mobilisation.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ko_relation += 3; june_march_preparation = 4; organiser_energy -= 2; party_unity += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "The democratic march gains a distinct red column"

Red banners enter Warsaw as an organised column, carrying trade-union and civil-
rights demands into a demonstration called by Tusk. The march looks broader
than KO and Lewica is visible inside it, not behind it. That distinction costs
organisers and money now, but it gives our supporters a reason to call the day
theirs as well.

- @poland_hub: Continue


@may23_caution
title: Avoid becoming scenery for Tusk's leadership campaign
on-arrival: ko_relation -= 5; p2050_relation -= 2; june_march_preparation = 0; organiser_energy += 2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.15; news_headline = "The Left keeps its distance from the 4 June march"

Lewica refuses the role of supporting cast in Tusk's return to centre stage.
Its organisers save their strength and its logo avoids absorption into KO's
campaign. On 4 June, however, the cameras find a democratic opposition larger
than us and a red absence easier to explain than our caution.

- @poland_hub: Continue


